  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is shown to interact with P2X purinoceptors, which are ionotropic receptors that mediate cellular signaling through purine ligand binding. This interaction is supported by the presence of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a compound that is a known target of Mollicellin N and is also a known inhibitor of P2X receptors. This compound is a common intermediate in the pathway leading to SF-188, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of P2X receptors. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent relationship between Mollicellin N and SF-188, with the shared target [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate acting as a bridge in the pathway. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong and reliable mechanistic link, though the specific role of the compound in the pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
